  "reason": "The strongest completed configuration is RNA multiprofile scvi_n200 with avgpool, with validation accuracy 0.650 and F1 0.628, and avgpool also outperformed transformer for PCA. Image-only ResNet50 singleprofile is weak, so whether image features can add value is uncertain. This experiment tests whether adding image features to the best RNA configuration via simple concat fusion improves validation accuracy/F1 while keeping the RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation fixed. It is the best next use of budget because it exploits the strongest known direction and directly clarifies the key multimodal fusion question before moving to more complex image encoders or fusion variants."
